{"event_type":"review","id":"b7d068ec9fa82b8aff7d3bb1d272a8c543c4408ff3702e97b7e18c12a4ad1ce2","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T04:20:41Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b6e1e787d0d1f46e4ce4516e16b59b455e7d23f741fef2fc92c578768c2cc3d0","sha256":"b6e1e787d0d1f46e4ce4516e16b59b455e7d23f741fef2fc92c578768c2cc3d0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/404e261d681b7bc05807d2f8b2a74f81e1c2adb4a59bf8eb83650800d64de1ce","sha256":"404e261d681b7bc05807d2f8b2a74f81e1c2adb4a59bf8eb83650800d64de1ce"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f57ab939a174f46c8f25ee6581fcb70fe54654f0316aecf7082f8114babd68c7","sha256":"f57ab939a174f46c8f25ee6581fcb70fe54654f0316aecf7082f8114babd68c7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/491de0b9414b06b9d12fcbbb1ad4657e4a4954815feea395a6997e8649f43999","sha256":"491de0b9414b06b9d12fcbbb1ad4657e4a4954815feea395a6997e8649f43999"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/541884dd3aa0a0ffb00b561077dc18cd19ba137f296387d35820b2223b6d1378","sha256":"541884dd3aa0a0ffb00b561077dc18cd19ba137f296387d35820b2223b6d1378"}],"attempt_id":"65be0be97c4bbb46c290e3641e928b3e946a19b563d3459224666c6a80c0ca36:0:1","base":"e578b83c4a0b8fe6b457e33394e1c1a303741055","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"71fb45ac0feda63e158e3148978f52e3b76f6121","body":"**Keep `reportPath` out of `sanitizeObservation`.**\n\nLine 866 sanitizes every string in the report, including `report.reportPath`. Lines 874–875 then use that sanitized value as the write target and as the path passed to `addressOrdinaryReport`. `stripCredentialText` treats text before the last `@` in a whitespace-free run as a credential prefix. A journal path with `@` in a parent directory is therefore rewritten. For example, `/home/u/@work/.cq-address-runs/<uuid>/review-address-report.json` becomes the relative path `work/.cq-address-runs/<uuid>/review-address-report.json`. `writeFile` at line 874 then resolves that path against the process working directory. The directory normally does not exist there, so the catch branch at lines 876–878 returns `status: 'failed'`. The report is not persisted, and the returned `reportPath` names the wrong location.\n\nKeep the write target raw, as the engine owns it:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      Object.assign(report, sanitizeObservation(report));\n+      const reportPath = report.reportPath;\n+      Object.assign(report, sanitizeObservation(report));\n+      // The write target is engine-owned identity, not observational text.\n+      report.reportPath = reportPath;\n```\n</details>","id":"a37c786938fce2b438864f13458cf14d2797dd9063b9aa7faf733314e9d209d9","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/address.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep `reportPath` out of `sanitizeObservation`."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"71fb45ac0feda63e158e3148978f52e3b76f6121","body":"**Child-mode pin blocks round 2 after a pushed round-1 fix.**\n\n`src/ops/review/address.ts:2839-2841` passes `input.expectedHead` only when `round === 1`. `src/ops/review/address.ts:2848` passes `lease.expectedHead` in every round. That value is `child.selection.head` (`src/ops/review/internal/addressOwnership.ts:1185`), which does not change between rounds. The round loop at `src/ops/review/address.ts:2712` runs `policy.review.rounds` times, and this file has no child-specific round cap.\n\nWhen round 1 pushes a fix to the review branch, round 2 resolves a different head. `claimCheckout` (`src/ops/review/internal/addressOwnership.ts:1229-1233`) then throws `resolved identity changed`, and the head-refusal path at `src/ops/review/address.ts:2967-2968` can end the run as `PR head changed before dispatch`. Child-mode runs can therefore stop after a round-1 push.\n\nDecide the intended behavior first. If child mode should stop after one fix, document that and keep the round-1 limit. If child mode should continue, the pinned head must advance after round 1. Limiting `lease.expectedHead` to round 1 does not achieve this, because `claimCheckout` still compares against `child.selection.head`.","id":"95606b12bd36edf7a72bea97a174058c23fb09b74a2e8881582799b9867f65bf","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/address.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Child-mode pin blocks round 2 after a pushed round-1 fix."}],"head":"00fda68101f54b3d403eb1f296e103cbfc505fc0","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"71fb45ac0feda63e158e3148978f52e3b76f6121","intervals":[[1,2],[16,16],[25,26],[32,32],[34,34],[41,41],[47,47],[49,53],[55,65],[75,87],[89,115],[120,122],[132,133],[137,138],[146,167],[169,173],[179,189],[192,192],[208,249],[255,256],[263,267],[271,322],[336,339],[383,392],[398,404],[410,413],[426,571],[591,591],[603,614],[617,639],[661,684],[748,756],[759,762],[787,788],[834,866],[868,869],[871,875],[883,883],[894,902],[905,905],[921,923],[932,935],[943,943],[952,963],[975,1201],[1210,1210],[1213,1224],[1234,1236],[1238,1238],[1242,1242],[1248,1251],[1256,1270],[1281,1284],[1286,1340],[1342,1390],[1392,1392],[1394,1394],[1397,1426],[1428,1431],[1434,1436],[1438,1447],[1449,1449],[1454,1460],[1462,1462],[1467,1535],[1537,1550],[1552,1909],[1912,1913],[1918,1926],[1928,2073],[2075,2099],[2101,2109],[2112,2115],[2117,2157],[2159,2172],[2175,2182],[2184,2225],[2227,2229],[2231,2234],[2236,2437],[2439,2449],[2451,2680],[2682,2977],[2982,3020],[3022,3028],[3032,3041],[3043,3067],[3069,3102],[3104,3188],[3190,3229],[3231,3240],[3243,3245],[3248,3248],[3250,3278],[3281,3282],[3284,3314],[3316,3321],[3323,3344]],"path":"src/ops/review/address.ts"},{"blob":"c1509673156cf00aa5a917c295166f32e904b9bc","intervals":[[1,1],[8,8],[58,63